            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A system includes: an interbody spacer (600), the interbody spacer (600) being expandable and including: a first body portion (602) and a second body portion (604) pivotably coupled via a rod (606), each of the first body portion (602) and the second body portion (604) defining a bone screw mount (610, 612) offset from a plane perpendicular to a pivot axis (B-B) defined by the rod (606); a pawl beam (614) rotatably coupled to the second body portion (604); and a plurality of teeth (616a) extending from an engagement wall (616), the plurality of teeth (616a) configured to engage the pawl beam (614), wherein transitioning the expandable interbody spacer (600) from a closed configuration to an open configuration causes the pawl beam (614) to engage the plurality of teeth (616a) to prevent the expandable interbody spacer (600) from transitioning towards the closed configuration.</p>
            </abstract>
